  "markdown_content": "## Policy Changes in Indian Gas Procurement\\n\\nIndia has introduced significant changes to its gas procurement policy affecting fertiliser companies, allowing them to source about 20% of their monthly gas requirements through the local spot market. The move represents a strategic shift in procurement practices aimed at reducing the government's substantial subsidy burden.\\n\\nThe policy adjustment comes as part of broader efforts to optimize costs in the fertiliser sector, where gas serves as a crucial raw material. Previously, fertiliser companies had more restricted procurement options, but this new flexibility could potentially lead to more cost-effective purchasing decisions.\\n\\nThe government sources indicate that this change is expected to result in meaningful savings on the national subsidy bill, which has been under pressure due to volatile global energy prices.",
